 "question": "The curve is f(x) = x² and the tangent touches it at a = 1. How do I find the tangent line y = mx + b?",
 "reference_answer": "Point of tangency: f(1) = 1, so (1, 1). Derivative f'(x) = 2x, so the slope m = f'(1) = 2. b = f(a) − m·a = 1 − 2 = −1. Tangent line: y = 2x − 1 (it crosses the y-axis at −1, as on the graph).",
